Package: cybroid-edition-security
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: CybroidOS maintainers <citos@cybroid.com>
Homepage: https://cybroid.com/cybroidos
Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Depends: cybroid-plasma (>= @VERSION@), nmap, zenmap, tshark, wireshark, tcpdump, masscan, gobuster, ffuf, nikto, whatweb, wafw00f, sslscan, testssl.sh, sqlmap, hydra, john, hashcat, hashid, crunch, cewl, aircrack-ng, hcxtools, hcxdumptool, reaver, bettercap, python3-impacket, python3-pwntools, smbclient, onesixtyone, sleuthkit, autopsy, foremost, testdisk, gddrescue, libimage-exiftool-perl, steghide, yara, binwalk, edb-debugger, lynis, rkhunter, proxychains4, tor, macchanger, wireguard-tools, openvpn, keepassxc, socat, netcat-openbsd, whois, bind9-dnsutils, podman, distrobox
Description: CybroidOS Security: for analysts and security teams
 Assessment, web, password, wireless and forensics tools from Debian: Nmap
 and Zenmap, Wireshark, tcpdump, masscan; Gobuster, ffuf, Nikto, WhatWeb,
 sslscan and testssl.sh; sqlmap, Hydra, John the Ripper, hashcat;
 Aircrack-ng, hcxtools, Reaver and Bettercap; Impacket and pwntools; The
 Sleuth Kit with Autopsy, TestDisk, foremost, ExifTool, YARA and binwalk;
 Lynis and rkhunter; Tor, ProxyChains, WireGuard, OpenVPN and KeePassXC.
 Kali's own tools (Metasploit, Responder, NetExec, radare2) run in a
 container: "Kali tools" in Launchpad creates it on first use (Distrobox
 and Podman). Burp Suite, ZAP and Ghidra install from the App Centre.
 .
 The same CybroidOS as every edition (look, updates, Hangar), with these
 tools added. An installed CybroidOS becomes this edition by installing this
 package; several editions can be installed together.
